sequenceDiagram
    participant P as Primary (WalSender)
    participant N as Network
    participant S as Standby (WalReceiver)

    Note over P,S: PostgreSQL Streaming Replication Protocol Messages

    %% Connection Establishment
    S->>+N: libpq connection
    N->>+P: TCP connection established
    P-->>-N: Connection acknowledged
    N-->>-S: Connection ready

    S->>+N: Authentication
    N->>+P: Auth request
    P-->>-N: Auth response
    N-->>-S: Authentication complete

    %% Replication Protocol Initiation
    S->>+N: START_REPLICATION command
    Note right of S: START_REPLICATION slot_name start_lsn timeline

    N->>+P: Parse START_REPLICATION
    P->>P: Validate parameters
    P->>P: Switch to Copy protocol
    P-->>-N: CopyBothResponse
    N-->>-S: Copy protocol active

    %% WAL Data Streaming
    loop Continuous WAL Streaming
        P->>+N: CopyData - WAL Record
        Note right of P: Message format:<br/>- 'w' (WAL data)<br/>- WAL start LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- WAL end LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- Send timestamp (8 bytes)<br/>- WAL record data

        N->>+S: WAL data received
        S->>S: XLogWalRcvProcessMsg()
        S->>S: Write WAL to disk
        S->>S: Flush WAL to storage
        S-->>-N: WAL processed
        N-->>-P: Processing complete

        %% Keepalive Messages
        alt Keepalive Needed
            P->>+N: CopyData - Keepalive
            Note right of P: Message format:<br/>- 'k' (keepalive)<br/>- WAL end LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- Send timestamp (8 bytes)<br/>- Reply requested (1 byte)

            N->>+S: Keepalive received
            S->>S: Process keepalive
            S-->>-N: Keepalive processed
            N-->>-P: Keepalive acknowledged
        end

        %% Standby Status Replies
        alt Status Interval Reached
            S->>+N: CopyData - Standby Reply
            Note left of S: Message format:<br/>- 'r' (reply)<br/>- Write LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- Flush LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- Apply LSN (8 bytes)<br/>- Timestamp (8 bytes)<br/>- Reply requested (1 byte)

            N->>+P: Status reply received
            P->>P: ProcessStandbyReplyMessage()
            P->>P: Update standby positions
            P->>P: SyncRepReleaseWaiters()
            P-->>-N: Reply processed
            N-->>-S: Reply acknowledged
        end

        %% Hot Standby Feedback
        alt Hot Standby Active
            S->>+N: CopyData - HS Feedback
            Note left of S: Message format:<br/>- 'h' (hs feedback)<br/>- Timestamp (8 bytes)<br/>- xmin (4 bytes)<br/>- xmin epoch (4 bytes)<br/>- catalog_xmin (4 bytes)<br/>- catalog_xmin_epoch (4 bytes)

            N->>+P: HS feedback received
            P->>P: ProcessStandbyHSFeedbackMessage()
            P->>P: Update replication slots
            P-->>-N: Feedback processed
            N-->>-S: Feedback acknowledged
        end
    end

    %% Error Scenarios
    alt Network Error
        N->>P: Connection lost
        P->>P: Cleanup resources
        P->>P: Log disconnection

        N->>S: Connection lost
        S->>S: WalRcvDie()
        S->>S: Attempt reconnection
    end

    alt Protocol Error
        S->>+N: Invalid message
        N->>+P: Protocol violation
        P->>P: ereport(FATAL)
        P->>P: proc_exit(0)
        P-->>-N: Connection terminated
        N-->>-S: Connection closed
    end

    alt Timeline Switch
        P->>+N: CopyData - Timeline History
        Note right of P: Timeline change detection<br/>Send timeline history files

        N->>+S: Timeline data
        S->>S: Process timeline switch
        S->>S: Validate timeline consistency
        S-->>-N: Timeline switch complete
        N-->>-P: Continue streaming
    end

    %% Graceful Shutdown
    S->>+N: CopyDone
    Note left of S: Request streaming termination

    N->>+P: CopyDone received
    P->>P: Stop streaming
    P->>P: Send final CopyDone
    P-->>-N: CopyDone sent
    N-->>-S: Streaming terminated

    S->>+N: Terminate ('X')
    N->>+P: Connection termination
    P->>P: Clean shutdown
    P-->>-N: Connection closed
    N-->>-S: Connection closed

    %% Message Size and Frequency Analysis
    Note over P,S: Message Characteristics
    Note right of P: WAL Data Messages:<br/>- Variable size (1KB - 1MB typical)<br/>- High frequency during peak load<br/>- Batched for efficiency

    Note left of S: Status Messages:<br/>- Fixed size (34 bytes reply, 25 bytes HS)<br/>- Low frequency (10-30 second intervals)<br/>- Minimal overhead

    Note over N: Network Optimization:<br/>- TCP Nagle disabled for low latency<br/>- Large send/receive buffers<br/>- Keep-alive for connection monitoring

    %% Protocol State Tracking
    Note over P,S: Protocol State Management
    Note right of P: Primary tracks:<br/>- Last sent position<br/>- Standby acknowledged positions<br/>- Synchronous replication waiters

    Note left of S: Standby tracks:<br/>- Last received position<br/>- Last written/flushed positions<br/>- Last applied position

    %% Performance Considerations
    Note over P,S: Performance Optimizations
    Note over P,S: - Non-blocking I/O operations<br/>- Batch message processing<br/>- Adaptive keepalive intervals<br/>- Efficient binary protocol<br/>- Compression for WAL data (future)